*PPD-Adobe: "4.3"
*% Label Proxy: an AirPrint queue that accepts anything and hands a cropped,
*% label-sized PDF to the labelcrop backend.
*%
*% The two keywords that make iOS treat this as an AirPrint printer are
*% cupsUrfSupported (becomes URF= in the Bonjour TXT record, without which iOS
*% ignores the queue entirely) and the cupsFilter2 line (becomes pdl=). Values
*% mirror what the QL-1110NWB itself advertises, since that is what ultimately
*% prints: 300dpi, 8-bit greyscale, one copy per pass.
*FormatVersion: "4.3"
*FileVersion: "2.0"
*LanguageVersion: English
*LanguageEncoding: ISOLatin1
*PCFileName: "LBLPROXY.PPD"
*Manufacturer: "Brother"
*Product: "(Brother QL-1110NWB)"
*ModelName: "Brother QL-1110NWB"
*ShortNickName: "Brother QL-1110NWB"
*NickName: "Brother QL-1110NWB"
*PSVersion: "(3010.000) 0"
*LanguageLevel: "3"
*ColorDevice: False
*DefaultColorSpace: Gray
*FileSystem: False
*Throughput: "1"
*LandscapeOrientation: Plus90
*TTRasterizer: Type42
*cupsVersion: 2.4
*cupsModelNumber: 0
*cupsManualCopies: False

*% Accept anything CUPS can turn into PDF: application/pdf, image/jpeg,
*% image/png, image/urf, text/plain. The backend gets PDF in every case.
*cupsFilter2: "application/vnd.cups-pdf application/pdf 0 -"

*% AirPrint advertisement. V1.4 = URF version, W8 = 8-bit greyscale,
*% CP1 = one copy per pass, RS300 = 300dpi, IS1 = main input slot,
*% MT1-5 = media types, OB10 = output bin, PQ4 = normal quality,
*% DM1 = one-sided only.
*cupsUrfSupported: "V1.4,W8,CP1,IS1,MT1-5,OB10,PQ4,RS300,DM1"
*APSupplies: "source=none"

*% NOTE: there is deliberately no *APPrinterIconPath here. It is a macOS-CUPS
*% keyword and Debian's cupsd ignores it entirely - the binary contains no
*% reference to it, nor any per-printer icon handling. The icon is installed as
*% doc-root/images/generic.png instead; see setup.sh and the README.
*cupsSNMPSupplies: False

*% Identity is copied verbatim from the real QL-1110NWB so macOS/iOS draw the
*% label-printer icon rather than the generic laser one. ty= comes from NickName
*% and product= from Product, and those are the keys the OS matches on; usb_MFG/
*% usb_MDL cannot be reproduced here because stock CUPS only emits them for
*% usb:// device URIs, not network queues.
*%
*% This does NOT rename what you see: the queue's display name comes from the
*% Bonjour service name ("Label Printer (auto-crop) @ labelproxy") and the -D
*% description, both of which stay distinct from the real printer.
*%
*% Makes macOS/iOS draw the QL-1110NWB icon instead of the generic laser one.
*% CUPS turns this into usb_MFG= / usb_MDL= in the Bonjour TXT record, which is
*% what the OS matches against its printer icon database. Copied from the real
*% printer's own printer-device-id. Cosmetic only - it does not change routing,
*% and the service name and UUID still differ from the real queue.
*1284DeviceID: "MFG:Brother;CMD:PT-CBP,URF;MDL:QL-1110NWB;CLS:PRINTER;CID:Brother QL Type1;"

*OpenUI *PageSize/Media Size: PickOne
*OrderDependency: 10 AnySetup *PageSize
*DefaultPageSize: Label103x164
*PageSize Label103x164/Label 103 x 164 mm: "<</PageSize[292 465]>>setpagedevice"
*PageSize A4/A4: "<</PageSize[595 842]>>setpagedevice"
*PageSize Letter/US Letter: "<</PageSize[612 792]>>setpagedevice"
*CloseUI: *PageSize

*OpenUI *PageRegion/Media Size: PickOne
*OrderDependency: 10 AnySetup *PageRegion
*DefaultPageRegion: Label103x164
*PageRegion Label103x164/Label 103 x 164 mm: "<</PageSize[292 465]>>setpagedevice"
*PageRegion A4/A4: "<</PageSize[595 842]>>setpagedevice"
*PageRegion Letter/US Letter: "<</PageSize[612 792]>>setpagedevice"
*CloseUI: *PageRegion

*% Full-bleed imageable areas. The real unprintable margins belong to the
*% Brother and are applied by the backend when it places content, not here,
*% so that iOS does not shrink the page a second time.
*DefaultImageableArea: Label103x164
*ImageableArea Label103x164/Label 103 x 164 mm: "0 0 292 465"
*ImageableArea A4/A4: "0 0 595 842"
*ImageableArea Letter/US Letter: "0 0 612 792"

*DefaultPaperDimension: Label103x164
*PaperDimension Label103x164/Label 103 x 164 mm: "292 465"
*PaperDimension A4/A4: "595 842"
*PaperDimension Letter/US Letter: "612 792"

*OpenUI *Resolution/Resolution: PickOne
*OrderDependency: 20 AnySetup *Resolution
*DefaultResolution: 300dpi
*Resolution 300dpi/300 dpi: "<</HWResolution[300 300]>>setpagedevice"
*CloseUI: *Resolution
